=== RETEST: correct show command on the PEER ===
`show bgp ipv6 unicast` is not valid on the AR4050S; the wiki page is
show-bgp-ipv6-bgp4-only.md, i.e. the command is `show bgp ipv6`.

--- peer: show bgp ipv6  [ok] ---
--- peer: show ipv6 route bgp  [ok] ---
    Gateway of last resort is not set
    No entries in route table

show bgp ipv6 neighbors 2001:db8:10::2 advertised-routes


IE520-stk#--- DUT: routes ADVERTISED to the peer ---
    => DUT is advertising ::/0 to the peer: False

VERDICT: see tables above

=== CAUSE FOUND: cross-case interference from T3112, not a product fault ===
T3112 applied an outbound prefix-list to this same neighbour containing
    seq 10 deny ::/0 le 128
which explicitly denies the default route outbound. T3111 was then asking the
DUT to advertise ::/0 through a filter built to block it. Two cases sharing
one live session -- the earlier one's config must be removed first.

configure terminal
Enter configuration commands, one per line.  End with CNTL/Z.
IE520-stk(config)#router bgp 65001
IE520-stk(config-router)#address-family ipv6
IE520-stk(config-router-af)#no neighbor 2001:db8:10::2 prefix-list PL-OUT out
IE520-stk(config-router-af)#exit-address-family
IE520-stk(config-router)#exit
IE520-stk(config)#end
IE520-stk#--- remove the T3112 prefix-list binding: ok ---
